{"lines": ["In November 1872, Captain Benjamin Briggs sailed the Mary Celeste out of New York, bound for Genoa, Italy.", "With him were his wife Sarah, their two-year-old daughter Sophia, and seven crew.", "A month later, another ship spotted her between the Azores and Portugal, sailing unsteadily under partial sail.", "Sailors rowed over and climbed aboard, and found no one.", "The cargo of 1,701 barrels of alcohol was intact.", "Belongings were untouched, and food was still plentiful.", "The only lifeboat was gone.", "The last log entry was nine days old, written almost 400 nautical miles away.", "And most of the ship's papers were gone, along with the captain's navigation instruments.", "In Gibraltar, an official suspected murder, but tests showed the stains found on board were not blood.", "One idea is that fumes from the alcohol scared Briggs into abandoning a ship that could still sail.", "None of the ten people was ever seen again.", "Now remember those missing instruments, because forty-nine years later, it happened again."], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.1], ["November", 0.1, 0.38], ["1872,", 0.38, 2.82], ["Captain", 3.26, 3.68], ["Benjamin", 3.68, 4.2], ["Briggs", 4.2, 4.54], ["sailed", 4.54, 5.14], ["the", 5.14, 5.34], ["Mary", 5.34, 5.58], ["Celeste", 5.58, 6.1], ["out", 6.1, 6.44], ["of", 6.44, 6.58], ["New", 6.58, 6.74], ["York,", 6.74, 7.1], ["bound", 7.6, 7.9], ["for", 7.9, 8.26], ["Genoa,", 8.26, 8.68], ["Italy.", 9.2, 9.25], ["With", 9.84, 10.02], ["him", 10.02, 10.16], ["were", 10.16, 10.38], ["his", 10.38, 10.52], ["wife", 10.52, 10.7], ["Sarah,", 10.7, 11.08], ["their", 11.52, 11.7], ["two-year-old", 11.7, 12.5], ["daughter", 12.5, 12.8], ["Sophia,", 12.8, 13.18], ["and", 13.7, 13.92], ["seven", 13.92, 14.2], ["crew.", 14.2, 14.5], ["A", 15.08, 15.18], ["month", 15.18, 15.34], ["later,", 15.34, 15.74], ["another", 16.18, 16.38], ["ship", 16.38, 16.7], ["spotted", 16.7, 17.1], ["her", 17.1, 17.32], ["between", 17.32, 17.62], ["the", 17.62, 17.76], ["Az